                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p141-q34-b-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "The inner function takes every value in ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "[0,1]",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "; these are all valid inputs of ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "f",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " and give outputs from ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "\\frac12",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " to ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "1",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ".",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "The square root requires\n$$\\begin{align*}1-x^2&\\ge0\\\\x^2&\\le1\\\\-1&\\le x\\le1.\\end{align*}$$\nOn this domain, $g$ takes every value in $[0,1]$. Since $\\operatorname{dom}(f)=\\mathbb{R}\\setminus\\{2\\}$,\n$$\\operatorname{range}(g)\\cap\\operatorname{dom}(f)=[0,1].$$\nEvery output of $g$ is therefore a valid input of $f$, so the composite domain is $[-1,1]$.\n\nFor these inputs,\n$$\\begin{align*}1&\\le2-g(x)\\le2\\\\\\frac12&\\le\\frac{1}{2-g(x)}\\le1.\\end{align*}$$\nAs $g(x)$ takes every value from $0$ to $1$, $f(g(x))$ takes every value from $\\frac12$ to $1$. Both endpoints are attained: $g(\\pm1)=0$ and $g(0)=1$.\n\nTherefore, the domain is $[-1,1]$ and the range is $\\left[\\frac12,1\\right]$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 62
      }
    ]
